{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 COLLECTION — WINNING-SPEC 4.6 "the four numbers"  ·  #env2-coll-terms  ·  section 6 of 7.

  4.6 in one line: the PDP's terms ledger, lifted onto the collection page as a 2-COLUMN HAIRLINE
  LEDGER — never four boxes. The shape the winner gets wrong on mobile is a 2x2 bordered grid
  (evening shot-mobile.png, slice 4); this file cannot draw one: the ledger is a two-column grid
  (numeral | term) with four full-width rows on hairlines, and under 900px it is one column.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- the copy, and where it comes from
  The four numbers are the LICENSED consumer wording, verbatim from 4.6 and identical to the PDP's
  4.6 and to the homepage terms strip. No new claim is written here and no product field is read, so
  this section renders correctly and identically on all five collection URLs:

    0     - 4 -  משלוח לנקודת איסוף — חינם. עד הבית 29.90 ₪.
    8-17  - 4 -  ימי עסקים לאספקה: 1–3 ימי טיפול ו־7–14 ימי משלוח. ייתכן משלוח ממחסן מחוץ לישראל.
    14    - 4 -  יום לביטול מקבלת המוצר, לפי חוק הגנת הצרכן. דמי ביטול עד 5% או 100 ₪ — הנמוך מביניהם.
    1     - 4 -  תמונה — שולחים תמונה של המקום ואנחנו בודקים התאמה לפני ההזמנה.

  Each row is numeral + unit + a bold licensed headline + the licensed sentence, so the 4.6 string
  reads back in its own order once the layout supplies the space between the numeral and the words.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ONE number that is Liquid
  Everything above is store terms, not catalogue data, so nothing above may be derived. The one
  figure on this screen that IS the collection's own is the deck's count, and it is never typed:
  the merchant writes [count] and Liquid substitutes collection.products_count (7 / 8 / 6 / 6 / 27),
  wrapped in bdi like every other numeral on the page. When there is no collection in scope, or it
  is empty, the count sentence is not printed at all — deck_no_count is used instead, so the page can
  never say "0 המנורות". This is the whole of 6.19 that applies to a section of licensed wording.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- the photo link (4.6 mailto rule)
  settings.whatsapp_number is empty, so the call to action is a mailto and the word for the other
  channel can not appear: this file never builds the URL and never writes the label — it renders
  snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-photo-cta with style 'ghost', the one place both branches live, which
  strips any such claim from a label a merchant types. The prefilled body names the COLLECTION
  (the PDP names the product), which is the second and last thing Liquid contributes here.
  The note sits beside it, as 4.6 asks: כאשר מידע אינו מאומת, איננו מציגים אותו כעובדה.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- core REPORT 9.1
  The core's .env2-section a{color:inherit} is (0,1,1) and outranks .env2-btn{color} (0,1,0), so an
  ANCHOR styled as the filled pill renders ink-on-glow at 1.21:1. There is no filled pill in this
  section: the only control is the outlined ghost, and its colour is set from this section's own
  (0,2,0) selector so it can not inherit anything else. Measured in _verify-terms.js: 0 failures.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- bidi
  Every digit-leading token of a headline, a sentence or the deck is wrapped in bdi at render time,
  so "1–3" never flips to "3–1" inside a Hebrew sentence and "8–17" keeps its order. The wrapper
  splits on spaces and never inside a token, so a slash pair stays inside ONE bdi (6.17). It runs
  ONCE over the deck and all four rows joined, which is why the model is built and split below.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------- no JS / reduced motion
  Everything is server-rendered text. With JavaScript disabled the four numerals are lit (the core
  sets --lit:1 unless html.env2-js), every licensed sentence is present, and the two link kinds are
  ordinary anchors — the ghost is a mailto and the foot links are plain hrefs. JS does exactly one
  thing: light the four numerals in reading order, 120ms apart (3.3). That is why the rows are
  data-lamp="manual" — the core's shared observer skips manual lamps, except under reduced motion,
  where it lights all four at once with no transition.

  Plumbing: elmsnest-v2-core (rendered by layout/theme.liquid on every template) supplies the
  tokens, the fonts, the .env2-* helpers and window.env2. The night ground is painted by
  elmsnest-v2-ground-collection, which elmsnest-v2-coll-scene renders once. This section renders no
  global, paints no background, owns no image, reads no option axis and prints no price.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign digits = '0123456789'
  assign line_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'number'

  assign env2_count = 0
  if collection != blank and collection.products_count != blank
    assign env2_count = collection.products_count | plus: 0
  endif

  assign env2_deck_src = section.settings.deck
  if env2_count < 1 or env2_deck_src == blank
    assign env2_deck_src = section.settings.deck_no_count
  endif
  assign env2_count_txt = env2_count | append: ''
  assign env2_deck_src = env2_deck_src | default: '' | replace: '[count]', env2_count_txt

  # ONE bidi pass over the deck and all four rows: deck ~~R~~ headline ~~F~~ sentence ~~R~~ …
  # Built with append rather than literal text so Shopify's whitespace trimming can not eat the
  # separators, and every piece is escaped before a bdi is injected into it.
  assign env2_src = env2_deck_src | strip
  for env2_b in line_blocks
    assign env2_src = env2_src | append: ' ~~R~~ ' | append: env2_b.settings.headline | append: ' ~~F~~ ' | append: env2_b.settings.sub
  endfor
  assign env2_out = ''
  assign env2_words = env2_src | strip | escape | split: ' '
  for w in env2_words
    assign c = w | slice: 0, 1
    if c != blank and digits contains c
      assign tok = '<bdi>' | append: w | append: '</bdi>'
    else
      assign tok = w
    endif
    if forloop.first
      assign env2_out = tok
    else
      assign env2_out = env2_out | append: ' ' | append: tok
    endif
  endfor
  assign env2_out = env2_out | replace: '</bdi> ₪', '</bdi>&nbsp;₪' | replace: '</bdi> %', '</bdi>&nbsp;%'
  assign env2_parts = env2_out | split: '~~R~~'
  assign env2_deck = env2_parts[0] | strip

  assign env2_mail_body = 'שלום, מצרף/ת תמונה של המקום שרוצים להאיר.'
  if collection != blank and collection.title != blank
    assign env2_mail_body = env2_mail_body | append: ' הקולקציה ששוקלים: ' | append: collection.title
  endif
-%}
<section id="env2-coll-terms" data-env2-coll-terms class="env2-section env2-coll env2-coll-terms" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px;--env2-stars:.55"{% if section.settings.heading != blank %} aria-labelledby="env2-coll-terms-h2"{% endif %}>
  <div class="env2-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="env2-wrap env2-coll-terms__wrap">
    <div class="env2-coll-terms__head">
      <div class="env2-coll-terms__title">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-eyebrow env2-coll-terms__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 id="env2-coll-terms-h2" class="env2-h env2-coll-terms__h2">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if env2_deck != '' -%}
        <p class="env2-coll-terms__deck">{{ env2_deck }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if line_blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ol class="env2-coll-terms__ledger" data-env2-coll-terms-ledger>
        {%- for block in line_blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign env2_pair = env2_parts[forloop.index] | default: '' | split: '~~F~~'
            assign env2_head = env2_pair[0] | default: '' | strip
            assign env2_sub = env2_pair[1] | default: '' | strip
          -%}
          <li class="env2-coll-terms__line" data-lamp="manual" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="env2-coll-terms__t">
              {%- if block.settings.numeral != blank or block.settings.unit != blank -%}
                <span class="env2-coll-terms__n">
                  {%- if block.settings.numeral != blank -%}
                    <bdi class="env2-coll-terms__num">{{ block.settings.numeral }}</bdi>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if block.settings.unit != blank -%}
                    <small class="env2-coll-terms__unit">{{ block.settings.unit }}</small>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if env2_head != '' -%}
                <b class="env2-coll-terms__b">{{ env2_head }}</b>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            {%- if env2_sub != '' -%}
              <p class="env2-coll-terms__p">{{ env2_sub }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank or section.settings.cta_note != blank -%}
      <div class="env2-coll-terms__act">
        {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-coll-terms__cta">
            {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-photo-cta',
                label: section.settings.cta_label,
                style: 'ghost',
                subject: section.settings.mail_subject,
                body: env2_mail_body,
                class: 'env2-coll-terms__btn' -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.cta_note != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-coll-terms__note">{{ section.settings.cta_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.foot_links != blank -%}
      <nav class="env2-coll-terms__foot" aria-label="עמודי מדיניות">{{ section.settings.foot_links }}</nav>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* ---------- 4.6 collection terms: a 2-COLUMN hairline ledger — numeral | term ----------
   Two columns, four full-width rows, hairlines between; never four boxes, never a 2x2 grid, and
   never a horizontally scrolling table on a phone. The section paints no background: the ground is
   the pixel-measured body gradient from elmsnest-v2-ground-collection (3.1) and the only thing this
   file puts above it is the star layer, at the 3.1 depth for this position (.55). */
.env2-coll-terms{padding-block:120px 96px}
.env2-coll-terms__wrap{position:relative;z-index:1}

/* head: eyebrow + h2 at the start, the deck at the end, bottoms aligned. The deck is Hebrew body
   copy, so it is NOT text-align:end — in RTL that is flush-left and puts the ragged edge on the
   side the eye returns to; justify-self does the placing instead. */
/* the head runs the ledger's own two tracks, so the deck sits exactly over the sentence column */
.env2-coll-terms__head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,42ch);align-items:end;gap:24px clamp(28px,4vw,72px);margin-block-end:48px}
.env2-coll-terms__title{min-width:0}
.env2-coll-terms__eyebrow{margin-block-end:20px}
.env2-coll-terms__h2.env2-h{font-size:clamp(30px,4.2vw,60px);max-width:16ch}
.env2-coll-terms__deck{justify-self:start;max-width:42ch;margin:0 0 .3em;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:clamp(16px,1.4vw,20px);line-height:1.55;color:var(--env2-ink-2);text-wrap:balance}
.env2-coll-terms__deck bdi{unicode-bidi:isolate;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}

/* the ledger: a hairline above every row and ONE continuous rule closing it, so it stays closed
   whether the merchant keeps four numbers, three, or two. */
/* The ledger's TWO columns are "the number and what it is" at the start and "the sentence" at the
   end, on one shared baseline, four full-width rows on hairlines. Not four boxes, not a 2x2 grid
   (4.6), and not a table that has to scroll sideways on a phone: under 900px it is one column. */
.env2-coll-terms__ledger{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;border-block-end:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-coll-terms__line{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,42ch);gap:14px clamp(28px,4vw,72px);align-items:baseline;margin:0;padding-block:32px;border-block-start:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}

/* the numeral: FRL 500 tabular, glow, unit at .32em in ink-2. --lit is 0 only while html.env2-js
   has not lit this row yet; no JS and reduced motion are both 1, so it is never dim there. */
.env2-coll-terms__n{flex:none;min-inline-size:244px;white-space:nowrap;font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(46px,4.6vw,68px);line-height:.92;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--env2-glow);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;text-shadow:0 0 34px rgba(255,211,148,.22);opacity:calc(.34 + .66*var(--lit,1));transition:opacity 1.1s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
.env2-coll-terms__num{unicode-bidi:isolate;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.env2-coll-terms__unit{display:inline;font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:400;font-size:.32em;line-height:1;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--env2-ink-2);margin-inline-start:.26em;text-shadow:none}

/* the term: the licensed headline, then the licensed sentence. 18px / 15px, both above the 13px
   caption floor; the sentence is the legal wording and is never shortened. */
.env2-coll-terms__t{min-width:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:10px clamp(20px,2.4vw,34px)}
.env2-coll-terms__b{min-width:0;flex:1 1 20ch;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:500;font-size:18px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-coll-terms__p{margin:0;min-width:0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--env2-ink-2)}
.env2-coll-terms__b bdi,.env2-coll-terms__p bdi{unicode-bidi:isolate;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}

/* the call to action, in the numeral column, with the note beside it (4.6). The control is the
   OUTLINED ghost and its colour is set from this (0,2,0) selector, which outranks the core's
   .env2-section a{color:inherit} (0,1,1) — core REPORT 9.1. 48px tall, the 3.2 target. */
.env2-coll-terms__act{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,42ch);gap:16px clamp(28px,4vw,72px);align-items:center;padding-block:30px;border-block-end:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-coll-terms__cta{margin:0;line-height:1}
.env2-coll-terms .env2-btn--ghost{color:var(--env2-ink);min-block-size:48px}
.env2-coll-terms .env2-btn--ghost:hover,.env2-coll-terms .env2-btn--ghost:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-coll-terms__note{margin:0;min-width:0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--env2-mute)}

/* foot: the policy pages, quiet, hairline-underlined. 14px — the 3.2 floor for an
   information-bearing line, not the 12.5px the v1 footer strip used for the same nav. */
.env2-coll-terms__foot{margin-block-start:26px;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:400;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-coll-terms__foot p{margin:0}
/* The 44px tap-target floor (6.13) is bought with padding on BOTH viewports — a policy link is a
   link a thumb has to hit. A border-block-end would then float 12px under the word instead of
   underlining it, so the rule is a text-decoration, which tracks the glyphs whatever the padding. */
.env2-coll-terms__foot a{display:inline-block;color:inherit;padding-block:12px;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:4px;text-decoration-color:rgba(143,149,163,.55);transition:color .3s,text-decoration-color .3s}
.env2-coll-terms__foot a:hover,.env2-coll-terms__foot a:focus-visible{color:var(--env2-glow);text-decoration-color:var(--env2-glow)}

/* ---------- mobile: one column, four rows, no 2x2 grid, 44px+ tap targets ---------- */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-coll-terms{padding-block:72px 56px}
  .env2-coll-terms__head{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px;margin-block-end:28px}
  .env2-coll-terms__eyebrow{margin-block-end:14px}
  .env2-coll-terms__h2.env2-h{max-width:none}
  .env2-coll-terms__deck{justify-self:start;max-width:none;margin-block-end:0;font-size:16px;text-wrap:pretty}
  .env2-coll-terms__line{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px;padding-block:26px}
  .env2-coll-terms__n{min-inline-size:0;font-size:46px}
  .env2-coll-terms__t{gap:10px}
  .env2-coll-terms__b{flex:1 1 100%;font-size:17px}
  .env2-coll-terms__act{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px;padding-block:26px}
  .env2-coll-terms__cta .env2-btn{inline-size:100%}
  .env2-coll-terms__foot{line-height:1.5}
  .env2-coll-terms__foot a{padding-block:13px}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* 4.6 motion (3.3): "the four numerals, in reading order, 120 ms stagger" — the ONLY thing this
   file does. The section is complete without it: every word is server-rendered and the core sets
   --lit:1 whenever html.env2-js is absent or reduced motion is on, so the numerals are lit and the
   ledger is readable. The rows are [data-lamp="manual"] so the core's shared observer leaves the
   stagger here (it still lights all four at once under reduced motion, which is what 3.3 asks for).
   Ends with the CONTRACT's env2.observe fallback line. */
(function () {
  function init(el) {
    if (el.__env2CollTerms) return;
    el.__env2CollTerms = true;

    var lines = Array.prototype.slice.call(el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp="manual"]'));
    var lightLine = function (l) {
      if (!l || l.classList.contains('lit')) return;
      if (window.env2 && window.env2.light) { window.env2.light(l); } else { l.classList.add('lit'); }
    };
    var lightAll = function (stagger) {
      lines.forEach(function (l, i) {
        if (stagger) { window.setTimeout(function () { lightLine(l); }, i * 120); } else { lightLine(l); }
      });
    };
    var rm = (window.env2 && window.env2.rm) ||
      (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);

    if (!lines.length) {
      /* nothing to stagger */
    } else if (rm || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) {
      lightAll(false);
    } else {
      var target = el.querySelector('[data-env2-coll-terms-ledger]') || el;
      var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
        entries.forEach(function (en) {
          var tall = en.boundingClientRect.top < window.innerHeight * 0.6;
          if (en.isIntersecting && (en.intersectionRatio >= 0.25 || tall)) {
            lightAll(true);
            io.disconnect();
          }
        });
      }, { threshold: [0, 0.25, 0.6], rootMargin: '0px 0px -6%' });
      io.observe(target);
    }

    window.env2 ? env2.observe(el) : el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp]').forEach(function (l) { l.classList.add('lit'); });
  }
  function boot(root) {
    var scope = (root && root.querySelectorAll) ? root : document;
    scope.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-coll-terms]').forEach(init);
    if (scope !== document && scope.matches && scope.matches('[data-env2-coll-terms]')) init(scope);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { boot(document); });
  } else {
    boot(document);
  }
  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', function (e) { boot(e.target || document); });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "לפני שקונים",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "כותרת עליונה קטנה", "default": "אחרי הבחירה — התנאים" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "כותרת", "default": "ארבעה מספרים, לפני שמשלמים." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "deck", "label": "שורת פתיחה (בצד השני של הכותרת)", "default": "לא אותיות קטנות. אותם תנאים לכל [count] המנורות בקולקציה.", "info": "[count] מוחלף במספר המוצרים בקולקציה, אוטומטית. אין להקליד מספר." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "deck_no_count", "label": "שורת פתיחה כשאין קולקציה", "default": "לא אותיות קטנות. אותם תנאים לכל המנורות בחנות.", "info": "מוצגת במקום השורה שלמעלה כשהעמוד אינו עמוד קולקציה, או שהקולקציה ריקה." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "התמונה של המקום" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "טקסט הכפתור", "default": "לשלוח תמונה של המקום" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mail_subject", "label": "נושא המייל", "default": "בדיקת התאמה — תמונה של המקום" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "cta_note", "label": "ההערה שלצד הכפתור", "default": "כאשר מידע אינו מאומת, איננו מציגים אותו כעובדה." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "תחתית" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "foot_links", "label": "קישורי מדיניות בתחתית", "default": "<p><a href=\"/pages/shipping-delivery\">משלוחים ואספקה</a> · <a href=\"/pages/processing-time\">זמני טיפול</a> · <a href=\"/policies/refund-policy\">מדיניות ביטולים</a> · <a href=\"/pages/help-faq\">שאלות נפוצות</a></p>", "info": "פסקה אחת עם הקישורים לעמודי המדיניות, מופרדים בנקודה." }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "number",
      "name": "מספר",
      "limit": 4,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "numeral", "label": "המספר הגדול", "default": "14", "info": "לדוגמה: 0 · 8–17 · 14 · 1" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "unit", "label": "יחידה (מוצגת קטן ליד המספר)", "default": "יום" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "headline", "label": "השורה המודגשת", "default": "לביטול מקבלת המוצר, לפי חוק הגנת הצרכן." },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "sub", "label": "משפט ההסבר", "default": "דמי ביטול עד 5% או 100 ₪ — הנמוך מביניהם.", "info": "מספרים וטווחים (למשל 1–3) נשמרים בכיוון הנכון אוטומטית. זהו נוסח משפטי — אין לקצר אותו." }
      ]
    }
